1.9 (The MK6.1 release is comprised of results from several projects at) 93.6 396 P
(the Open Software Foundation \320 Research Institute. These projects are:) 72 382 T
(a.) 97.2 362 T
(General evolution of the microkernel interface.) 110.88 362 T
(b.) 97.2 342 T
(The MK6 performance improvement project, which has contrib-) 110.88 342 T
(uted the server collocation component of the release.) 110.88 328 T
(c.) 97.2 308 T
(The MK6 device driver asynchronous I/O model, which allows) 110.88 308 T
(task notification directly from interrupt context.) 110.88 294 T
(d.) 97.2 274 T
-0.66 (The NMK18 NoRMA project,which has contributed enhancements) 110.88 274 P
(to the multicomputer support component of the release.) 110.88 260 T
(e.) 97.2 240 T
(The RT2 real-time project, which has contributed fundamental) 110.88 240 T
(extensions to the kernel in support of real-time applications and) 110.88 226 T
(environments.) 110.88 212 T
(f.) 97.2 192 T
(The Microkernel Performance Suite.) 110.88 192 T
1.33 (Each of these projects, except for the general evolution of the inter-) 93.6 166 P
(face, is described in greater detail in the following sections.) 72 152 T
